From 890668359d6b81862162bc11b7136bb4fc8efea8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 20:18:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06932/11362] [outer-loop] wire rule-based live HUD-cell
 masking into StepwiseExplorer (E1)

A comparative gap analysis against the hidden-leaderboard 3rd-place solver
("just-explore", arXiv:2512.24156) found that StepwiseExplorer.hud_mask had
existed as a constructor parameter since before this change (already
consumed by _hash to collapse masked cells out of node identity) but was
never populated on the live path -- neither E3AgentPolicy nor
CarnotAgentPolicy ever computed or passed one. A ticking score/timer/step-
counter HUD cell made every tick look like a brand-new state to the live
dedup, the same state-explosion failure mode just-explore's own status-bar
masking exists to prevent.

Adds _compute_hud_mask_from_frame: a rule-based, zero-action-cost classifier
reusing ColorBlobSaliencePrior.is_status_bar_like (frame-edge-touching,
spans most of the frame's width, thin), computed from a single already-
observed frame -- NOT the probe-based arc_graph_explore.discover_hud_mask,
which burns up to 4 real actions from reset and is only viable offline
where resets are free (RHAE live scoring squares extra actions against the
human baseline).

Wired via a new auto_hud_mask flag on StepwiseExplorer, computed at most
once per instance (on the first observed frame, never refreshed mid-search
to avoid corrupting node identity), threaded through both E3AgentPolicy and
CarnotAgentPolicy, gated by SUBMITTED_AUTO_HUD_MASK_ENABLED (default False
pending offline validation, per the Phase Prototype + Empirical Validation +
Adversarial Check Discipline). Added to SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG for parity-
test coverage.

Added REQ-ARC-WMTE-5583 + 3 scenarios and 11 unit tests. Verified against a
real offline game (dc22, 64x64 mask) with no exceptions, and confirmed via
an isolated baseline worktree (HEAD before this change) that the 10
pre-existing test failures in the broader 53-file arc_competition_agent
regression sweep are byte-for-byte identical with and without this change
-- zero new regressions (335/345 passed both ways).

